is it wrong for an apple based channel  to say that i am more excited for the  galaxy note 22 i mean the s22 ultra than  the iphone 14 pro well we just ordered  ours in and i can't wait to get my hands  on it especially to do another blind  photo comparison challenge which are  super fun and they're super entertaining  so if you guys want to see another one  of those go ahead and click that  subscribe button down below now i'm also  going to be switching from my iphone and  going to the s22 ultra for at least two  weeks as we are testing it out but  potentially that could be my main phone  with my iphone becoming a side one  because i do still need it because of  seven specific reasons and the first one  is definitely the design now some of you  guys may know that this year i did not  go for the max model iphone for the  first time in years because the regular  13 pro had the same exact features so  why would i want this big s22 ultra well  even though the screen is bigger than  apples and the battery life is also  bigger as well as having additional  cameras and a built-in s-pen it still  weighs less than the iphone and it is  actually narrower as well meaning that  even though has a big screen it is still  easier to hold in the hand and of course  we had to go for the ultra model because  it has the best specs out of the whole  s22 lineup so if you want the most  features you have to go for that one now  i am so happy that they stuck with the  note design and now again with the  ability to fast charge up to technically  47 watts but of course most will use the  45 watt brick now i love this design and  i was sad to see samsung not release a  new note and just do the folds last year  with the rumors of the note lineup just  merging into the s series i thought they  were gonna keep it with that same  s-series look and just ruin the note but  thankfully they didn't do this and they  brought back the note design and now  that is the top line ultra series of the  s lineup and that just makes a whole lot  of sense i've owned many notes even the  very first one which i loved but this  design in my opinion is samsung's best  ever the s21 ultra is probably the most  ugly with a really terrible camera bump  in my opinion now i'm not sure if i like  the new design on the note better than  the previous one that had a single  camera bump but you guys let me know  your thoughts down below the second is  the screen now of course the screen is  very similar compared to b4 but it does  go down to one hertz to save battery  life and it's able to keep up 120 hertz  at the full quality instead of having to  compromise with the note 20 i actually  kept it at 60 hertz because i could  definitely tell the difference when you  lower the screen resolution especially  when you are reading text but what i'm  most excited for is the  1700 peak knit brightness display that  is crazy it's crazy that it's even  better than apple's xdr screens that hit  a thousand six hundred nits and i'm  excited to see how bright it gets when  you're watching hdr content and more so  than that how it does out in the sun  because they never reach the peak limit  when you're using it in normal sdr but  it should be better than before and the  third reason is videography  they are making this a huge point this  year now as far as the sensors and stuff  not a lot has changed but processing can  make a huge difference with the s20 when  they advertise 8k like crazy it actually  looked terrible even worse quality than  shooting 4k with the same phone because  of processing but with future iterations  they made it quite a bit better and with  the s21 ultra the ak video looked so  much better that we actually went ahead  and compared it to a professional 5 000  camera shooting 8k video and in good  lighting it really held its own  unfortunately it is still only 24 frames  per second which can make it choppy  sometimes but i still cannot wait to  test it out and with that i want to  check out the nitography that they're  calling it nighttime video now as you  guys know with photos processing over  the last few years an hdr stacking has  made quality so much better but when we  switch our iphones to video mode and low  light it still really suffers because  they don't have um the same processing  that you get with night mode photography  so i'm looking forward to seeing how  good this night video is in the real  world and of course with that we also  have the photography side which is  number four we've taken a few trips  within the last year and at those trips  i really wish that i had the telephoto  lens from the samsung camera in my  iphone the telephoto camera quality can  also get quite a bit better with  processing with digital zoom and of  course the iphone 13 did get a three  times zoom and it got quite a bit better  than the iphone 12 but it still cannot  compare to having an actual telescopic  camera and we also know that even the  iphone 14 will not get that kind of a  camera we have to wait at least till the  iphone 15. the s22 ultra also has that  three times camera just like the iphone  that helps out when you don't need to  zoom in that much and in the past they  have had issues with processing with  that camera and the smaller sensor but  processing should make this look quite a  bit better and i can't wait to test it  out and also the 108 megapixel mode  which same thing with processing uh you  didn't have as good dynamic range you  had other issues even though you had  more resolution and detail compared to  apple's 12 megapixel when you were in  that high-res mode it didn't look good  but processing should make this a lot  better and to make that processing  better we have the new four nanometer  snapdragon 8 gen 1 processor which is  the fifth reason now i don't think this  is as big of a deal as samsung wants you  to believe it is but it is really cool  to see a four nanometer processor be put  into a phone and of course that brings  out a lot of competition  to keep apple on its toes and not  slowing down with their bionic series  chips now cpu performance didn't get  that much better in single core and the  same thing with multi-core and it's  still behind apple quite a ways but the  real improvement comes in with graphics  performance we're seeing it increase  from 77 fps and gfx bench all the way up  to 115 which is a 50 percent improvement  in opengl and when geekerwon switched  over to vulcan it got an even bigger  improvement of 57 pretty much matching  the a15 in the iphone 13 which is a huge  increase in performance now apple has  always been ahead in benchmarks but of  course in a real world gaming test there  were a lot of times that the samsung  actually proved to be better so i can't  wait to test out my favorite mobile game  call of duty mobile but with that  performance increase we have a huge jump  in power usage as well this is likely  the most power usage in any smartphone  pretty much reaching tablet levels  basically the same amount of power as  apple's m1 which is crazy and with that  much power you have to be able to cool  it down and samsung does have really  good thermal solutions in their phones  way better than apple which is not doing  anything but with that much wattage you  are still gonna get throttling and  geeker 1 showed it off where it actually  slowed down to 66.8 percent of its full  performance under heavy stress tests now  that is pretty extreme and in real world  usage it probably won't be that much so  we will be doing another head-to-head  gaming comparison against the iphone 13  pro max so make sure you guys have  notifications enabled if you guys want  to see that number six is the s pen now  over the last six months or so i've been  really getting into taking notes from my  personal life my goals things i'm  working on and i really wanted the full  three to be a great device that can do  that for me and be a great phone but it  was just too big and it had other issues  as well and of course with the s21 not  having that slot like the note series  meant you had to have this janky flip  case that made a lot more bulky to be  able to actually keep your pen with you  but going back to this note it's all  built in and very useful so i'm really  going to be trying to make the most use  of the s pen and seven is the fact that  this might be possible this year because  i did not buy the pro max model i bought  the 13 pro which is much smaller lighter  easier to keep in your pocket as a  secondary phone and of course i'm really  stuck in apple's ecosystem i use a lot  of their exclusive features i'm loving  air tags i use um find my friends and my  items all the time and i have my apple  watch as well so i can't just get rid of  my iphone i do need it but now since i  won't have two huge phones it'll be a  lot easier to be able to keep that and  use something else so i'm super excited  to be able to test out the note 22 ultra  and use it  if you guys think the same let me know  down below we're going to get it in  we're going to do a ton of videos  head-to-head comparisons tests that you  guys don't see on other channels ones  that are fun and informative so click  that circle above if you guys want to  check that out and help us reach our  goal of 1 million subscribers and check  out one of those great videos right over  there that's been max and i will see you  in the next video  [Music]

